.TH FILESYNC 1 "March 2026" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filesync \- map and sync files across git checkouts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filesync
.RI [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.br
.B filesync
.RI [ help | \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B filesync
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filesync
is a Bash CLI that keeps file mappings in a per-project
.B .filesync/
directory (configuration, repos, and file rows). It discovers the project by walking parent directories from the current working directory, similar to
.BR git .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
Common subcommands include
.BR init ,
.BR check ,
.BR sync ,
.BR list ,
repo management
.RB ( repos ", " repo ", " repo-edit ),
and file mapping commands
.RB ( add ", " add-master ", " push ", " attach ", " detach ", " rm ),
and
.B update
to compare with upstream releases and optionally reinstall.
Run
.B filesync
with no arguments for a short summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .filesync/config.json
Merged over package defaults; toggles and path mode.
.TP
.I .filesync/repos.json
Array of repo definitions.
.TP
.I .filesync/files.json
Array of file mapping rows.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FILESYNC_PROJECT_ROOT
Project root directory.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_DIR
Path to the
.B .filesync
directory.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_UPDATE_REPO
For
.BR "filesync update" ,
GitHub
.I owner/repo
(default: upstream).
.TP
.B FILESYNC_INSTALL_PREFIX
For
.BR "filesync update --apply"
from a git checkout,
.B PREFIX
passed to
.BR "make install"
when autodetection is wrong.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full configuration notes are in the installed documentation or upstream
.I docs/configuration.md .
.SH AUTHORS
Written by AragusNZ; see upstream repository for details.
